cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these certificates, please cite the accompanying manuscript."
title: "Monostatic polyhedra: no mono-stable pentahedron, and 9 <= V_U <= 14 (code, certificates and verifiers)"
authors:
  - family-names: Mattioni
    given-names: Claudio
    email: claudio.mattioni@gmail.com
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: "0.1-review"
date-released: 2026-11-16
keywords:
  - monostatic polyhedra
  - mono-stable
  - mono-unstable
  - computer-assisted proof
  - semidefinite certificates
  - interval arithmetic
abstract: >-
  Computer-assisted proofs that every homogeneous convex pentahedron has at least two stable faces and
  that every homogeneous convex polyhedron with at most 8 vertices has at least two unstable vertices,
  and an explicit mono-unstable polyhedron with 14 vertices. The archive contains the certificates, the
  trusted verifiers, a one-command reproduction script and the manuscript sources.
